A data processor shall formulate and maintain a record of processing activities for 
each category of its activities, containing the minimum details as follows: 
(1) The name and information pertaining to the data processor and pertaining to  
the data processor’s representative, if a representative has been appointed; 
(2) The name and information pertaining to the data controller for whom the data processor 
carrying out its instruction or conducting on behalf of such data controller and pertaining to  
the data controller’s representative, if one has been appointed; 
(3) The name and information pertaining the data protection officer, including place of contact 
and methods of contact, if the data processor has designated a data protection officer; 
(4)  The categories or nature of the collection, use or disclosure of the personal data carried 
out by the data processor under the instruction of or on behalf of the data controller; including such 
actual personal data and their purposes of the collection, use or disclosure as assigned by 
the data controller; 
(5)  The types of persons or entities to whom personal data are disclosed in case of sending 
or transferring personal data to a foreign country;  
(6)  The description of the security measures pursuant to Section 40 paragraph one (2).

Section 39 
The Data Controller shall maintain, at least, the following 
records in order to enable the data subject and the Office to check upon, which can be either in 
a written or electronic form: 
(1) the collected Personal Data; 
(2) the purpose of the collection of the Personal Data in each category; 
(3) details of the Data Controller;  

(4) the retention period of the Personal Data; 
(5) rights and methods for access to the Personal Data, including the conditions 
regarding the  Person having the right to access the Personal Data and the conditions to access 
such Personal Data; 
(6) the use or disclosure under section  27 paragraph three;  
(7) the rejection of request or objection according to section 30 paragraph three, 
section 31 paragraph three, section 32 paragraph three, and section 36 paragraph one;  
(8) explanation of the appropriate security measures pursuant to section 37 (1).

Section 39 
The Data Controller shall maintain, at least, the following 
records in order to enable the data subject and the Office to check upon, which can be either in 
a written or electronic form: 
(1) the collected Personal Data; 
(2) the purpose of the collection of the Personal Data in each category; 
